A||||34||85fierogt||audio excursions||||1||
Z||000000||85fierogt||08-21-2001||05:55 PM||||aight guys im considering a new headunit for my baby (85 fiero gt) its all stock speakers in there and i was considering an alpine cda-7873 or the 7875  (http://www.onlinecarstereo.com/caraudio/category.asp?c=1&m=8) ok now i was told that this unit would blow my speakers i want to upgrade but not right away so here u see my dillema, help anyone?<BR>-brad||||reg||1
Z||000001||Mach10||08-21-2001||06:03 PM||||Uh, no.<BR>Whoever told you that is trying to sell you speakers. <P>The factory speakers will sound better with the new deck. They STILL won't go loud. The new deck will have the power to roast the speakers, but only if you abuse them. Remember that those speakers are most likely 12+ years old. The surrounds will be cracking and still, and the cones brittle. Don't worry, the speakers will distort way before you start cooking the voicecoils.<P>Keep it real, and the speakers will last for a while yet. I still recommend replacing them soon, as they won't do your new deck justice. On the other hand, only do what you can afford at the moment. No sense digging yourself into debt over a CAR STEREO.||||reg||6
Z||000002||85fierogt||08-21-2001||06:07 PM||||thanks bro, helped alot, just how loaud will i be able to go i mean i want to be able to hear my music with the windows down on the highway, untill i can get the sub and new drop in, BTW anyone got the dimmesnions of the dash speakers?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mach10||08-21-2001||06:13 PM||||Hard to say. You'd have to keep turning it up until the music starts to distort. Turn it down a notch. That's the point at which you should never go higher unless the song is quiet (Ah, the wonderful world of MP3s). <BR>Just listen for distortion. If it's distorting, it MAY not cook the coils, but it will for sure destroy the speaker cone and/or surround after a while.<P>EDIT:<BR>Oh, the fronts are always 4x10" YUCK.<BR>do what I did, and make a backing plate, and squeeze in a set of 5-1/4's<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Mach10 (edited 08-21-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000004||JayUSA77||08-21-2001||06:14 PM||||the dash is 4*10's and the the speakers by your head are 4*6's, i replaced mine with pioneers all around including the deck and they sound great.<BR>J<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
