Z||000011||Mach10||08-21-2001||06:47 PM||||It's premier... Try this link:<P> <A HREF="http://www.pioneerelectronics.com/Pioneer/CDA/CarProducts/CarProductDetails/0,1429,1485,00.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.pioneerelectronics.com/Pioneer/CDA/CarProducts/CarProductDetails/0,1429,1485,00.html</A> <P>That's my deck. Might be a little trickier to find than alpine, but I assure you, it's available.<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000012||fieronv||08-21-2001||06:55 PM||||Another option on your front speakers is to put a 4 inch mid and 3/4 inch tweeter and make a plate to fit in the 4x10 space. In my 85 I'm running Rockford's mounted on a plate that I made and the tonal separation in the front is exceptional. If your putting the stereo into an 85GT your rear channels are in the headrest and a after market stereo will not "blow" the speakers if you do not abuse (over distort) them. The only draw back that I can see with only using the stock speakers is a lack of low end bass response (subs). As for an Alpine head unit they are a good unit though they are over priced, check the specs of a head unit and find the one that fits your needs the best and go to a shop and listen to it (with out a separate amp) with similar speakers. Stereo equipment is mostly user preference unless you are going to measure it with a frequency meter, wave form analyzer, and spectrum analyzer. Good luck and I think you will be happy with a new head unit once you do a little homework.<BR>PS Don't always listen to a salesman they get paid by commission.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>85GT (twoloud)||||reg||1
Z||000013||Mach10||08-21-2001||07:07 PM||||Good call Fieronv.<BR>I've got a set of DHP-1395 5-1/5" up front, and they are awesome for mid-highs. I have a set of FanaticQ 4" mid-drivers in the pillars. (Got them at a 2000-stock clearout for $100.00. AWESOME deal!) My separation up front is as good as it will EVER get without separates. Nice thing, is that the whole setup LOOKS bone-stock. Nice and stealth. all my stuff works together to provide excellent full-range. I ALMOST didn't need a sub. Yeah. Right. I have an older plain-jane Kicker10 in a custom sealed box that moulds pefectly to the footwell in the passenger side. It's removeable too, in case I need to move someone really big.<P>I'm selling the box soon, 'cos I want to use that other sub (same kind) that I have lying around. If interested, mail me, or keep an eye out in the Mall section. It's a sealed, at ~.6 ft^3 Works great, no leaks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
