Z||000026||Joe Torma||08-21-2001||11:34 PM||||They sure do.  They are the 3ways  Send me a msg/email if you want them.<P>My suggestion is to look through Crutchfield(only place I've seen em) for the foam speaker enclosures.  The low end freq will be better with them.  Put some polyfill in them too.<P>My problem with the small components up front is you have no midbass...is why I stuck with the 4x10s. <P>I traded everything including the dash for the Premier 6 3/4 Reference Series components(the yellow Kevlar ones).  I will be competing in IASCA next year(since everything seems to be taking forever to finish).||||reg||1
Z||000027||sqoach||08-21-2001||11:47 PM||||I'll send you an e-mail in a few minutes. I've seen those foam baffle things on Crutchfield too. What I did in my other fiero was just stuff a bunch of polyfill down the openings. Seemed to work pretty good. I just need some bass. I've got 4x6s up front and in the rear (don't ask). I don't have my sub and amp hooked up because I might be selling them. Already sold the sub box. These will at least help out on the bass. 4x6s are hardly capable of producing anything worthy to be called bass.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||1
