Z||000034||Mach10||08-22-2001||01:28 AM||||I'll get some pictures up eventually. <BR>Th 5-1/4's WILL fit, but you need to cut the dash up just a little. You have to enlarge the speaker opening a bit. It's tight, but they do fit. Mostly it's trial and error with an x-acto knife until they drop it. Then you make a backing, using whatever you like, using the old 4x10 basket as a guide. Then cut out a hole to mount the 5-1/4. You'll be left with 2 peices. Bolt the speaker in, and you have a complete set. To minimize air-leaks, I put foam-tape around the exposed areas. Then I mounted the assembly, and stuffed the unused area with some filler (Chopped up sweat pants) to prevent rattling. Works great, fits fine. No one would EVER know that you spent 1/2 hour hacking at your dash with an X-acto.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
